@startuml

title Registering a definition, and resolving it when a run starts

participant "the owning component\n(definition and handlers)" as owner
participant "the workflow service" as service
participant "the registry\n(in process)" as registry
database "the run and step rows" as db
participant "the caller" as caller

owner -> service : provide the definition
service -> registry : register it at startup,\nkeyed by type name

note over registry
    Registering a type name that already
    exists replaces the entry. The deployed
    build is the version of the definition.
end note

... later, a start message arrives ...

caller -> service : publish the start message\n(workflow.v1.ops.start_workflow, naming the type)
service -> registry : find the type

alt the type is registered
    service -> service : build the step list once\n(request, tenant, correlation)
    service -> db : create the run, with the step count\nand the resolved step list
    service -> db : dispatch the first step
else the type is not registered
    service --> caller : refuse the start
end

note over service, db
    A restart reads the resolved step list from the
    run and never rebuilds it.
end note

@enduml
